hgPangenome test suite
======================

Tests for the pangenome mapping tool: the browser client (js/hgPangenome.js)
and the CGI proxy (hgPangenome.c).  Layered so that everything except the
end-to-end layer runs with no middleware and no browser.

Run everything that can run here:

    make test          # or: ./runTests.sh

Layers whose tool is missing SKIP rather than fail, so this is safe on a build
machine with no node (node is optional in kent - see NODEBIN in inc/common.mk)
and with no CGI binary built.  "make help" lists the targets.

Run just the unit layer:

    node unitTests.js          # exit 0 = all passed


Why node and not the js/test JsTestDriver setup
-----------------------------------------------
src/hg/js/test/ holds a JsTestDriver (2011) harness that needs java plus a
captured browser.  These tests are plain node with a hand-rolled assert runner
and DOM stub: no npm packages, no java, no browser, milliseconds to run, easy to
put in CI.  No new project dependencies are introduced.


Files
-----
testLib.js      Tiny table-driven test runner + assertions (suite/test/eq/
                deepEq/ok/isNull/contains, exit code for CI).
loadClient.js   Loads js/hgPangenome.js (and the mock) into a node vm with a
                minimal window/document stub, and returns the client's test
                exports.  With no page elements present the client's init()
                returns early, which is what unit tests want; pass ids:[...]
                for a working element tree (used by the render layer).
unitTests.js    LAYER 1: pure-function unit tests.
renderTests.js  LAYER 3: contract/rendering tests over canned responses.
mockMiddleware.py
                Stand-in middleware for Layer 2: configurable status/body/delay,
                and records every request (method, path, headers, body) as JSON
                lines so tests can assert what the CGI actually sent upstream.
proxyTests.sh   LAYER 2: CGI proxy tests.
runTests.sh     Runs the layers (skipping any whose tool is absent).
makefile        Standard kent entry point: make test / testWithCgi /
                updateAssemblies / help.

The haplotype -> assembly table
-------------------------------
js/hgPangenomeAssemblies.js is generated from the HPRC browser index CSV, which
is committed at hgPangenome/ucsc_browser_hprc_r2_v1.0.index.csv - so generating
it needs no network access and is reproducible.  The generated file records the
CSV's name, sha256 and upstream URL.  Regenerate with:

    make updateAssemblies        # runs makeAssemblyMap.py, then the tests

For a new HPRC release, add its index CSV beside the script and point
DEFAULT_SRC (or the command line) at it.


What Layer 2 covers (83 checks)
-------------------------------
Runs the compiled CGI as a real CGI (POST with a urlencoded body on stdin, GET
with QUERY_STRING) against mockMiddleware.py.

input caps       51 rejected / 50 accepted (boundary); over-long sequence
                 rejected and one exactly at the limit accepted; non-ACGTN and
                 RNA "U" rejected; lower case accepted; over-size body
                 rejected; malformed JSON rejected without aborting the CGI;
                 missing 'sequences', empty array, entry without a sequence,
                 empty sequence.  Each rejection also asserts the request was
                 NOT forwarded upstream.
request shaping  forwarded once, as POST, to /api/v1/map, with
                 Content-Type: application/json, payload byte-for-byte
                 identical, Accept and User-Agent set; poll forwarded as GET to
                 /api/v1/map/<job_id>; trailing slash in apiBase normalized;
                 middleware answer passed through.
auth             configured token sent as X-Pangenome-Token on both map and
                 poll; no header at all when unconfigured.
job_id guard     rejects "../../etc/passwd", "a/b", "a?x=1", "a&b", "a;b",
                 "a b", a full URL, "$(id)", an over-long id and a missing id -
                 and asserts none of them are forwarded; accepts the normal
                 [A-Za-z0-9._-] charset.
error mapping    400/401/403/429/500/503 surfaced as an error envelope naming
                 the status; non-JSON 200 passed through; unreachable
                 middleware reported clearly; a slow middleware times out
                 instead of hanging; missing apiBase reported on map and poll.
bot delay        with the bottleneck server pointed at a dead port, cmd=map
                 consults it (fails closed) while cmd=poll does not and still
                 works - i.e. submissions are rate-limited, polling is exempt.
non-API paths    an unknown cmd neither forwards upstream nor emits an API
                 error envelope.

Isolation: the test hg.conf files are standalone (they do NOT include the site
hg.conf), so Layer 2 never touches the shared bottleneck server, MySQL, or the
real middleware.  The CGI is located via $PG_CGI, else ../hgPangenome, else the
installed sandbox CGI; if none exists the layer SKIPs with instructions.


What Layer 1 covers (62 assertions groups)
------------------------------------------
parseInput      one-per-line and FASTA input; wrapped sequence lines; header
                name tokenizing; bare ">"; blank lines; CRLF and bare-CR;
                indented headers; data before the first header; line numbers.
validate        autogenerated names (seq_N); duplicate-name uniquifying;
                collisions with Object.prototype member names; lower-case
                input; N allowed; U/digits/punctuation rejected; empty
                sequence; per-sequence errors with line numbers; the 50
                boundary and the 51 rejection; configured maxSequences.
cigarRefSpan    M/D/N/=/X consume reference; I/S/H do not; missing and "*"
                CIGARs; multi-digit and mixed operations.
refDbFor        CHM13->hs1, GRCh38->hg38, GRCh37/hg19->hg19, case-insensitive;
                sample haplotypes and unknown names -> no assembly;
                Object.prototype names -> no assembly; refAssemblies override.
refBrowserInfo  0-based -> 1-based start conversion; CIGAR-derived end;
                position 0; numeric "#offset" subpath applied; unrecognized
                subpath -> no link; accession-style contigs; no link for
                sample haplotypes, failed surjections or missing fields.
fmt             null/undefined -> em dash, but 0 and "" are real values.
formEncode      percent-encoding of JSON payloads and of &, =, +, space, #.


The test hook in the client
---------------------------
js/hgPangenome.js ends with

    if (typeof module !== "undefined" && module.exports)
        module.exports = { ... };

In a browser "module" is undefined, so this is a no-op there.  Under node it
exposes the functions these tests exercise.  Keep it in sync when adding
functions worth testing.


Bugs this layer has already caught
----------------------------------
1. validate() used a plain {} as its seen-names map, so sequences named
   "constructor"/"toString" (truthy via the prototype chain) were renamed
   spuriously, and duplicate "__proto__" names were never deduplicated.
   Fixed with Object.create(null).
2. refDbFor() looked names up on an object literal without hasOwnProperty, so
   a haplotype sample named "constructor" resolved to Object.prototype's
   member instead of "no such assembly".  Fixed with a hasOwnProperty guard.
3. When the bottleneck (rate limiter) server was unreachable, the JSON API
   path answered with an HTML 500 page, which the browser showed as raw
   markup.  Fixed by catching the abort and emitting the error envelope, with
   the host/port detail going to the error log rather than to the user.
   Finding that also exposed a build problem: the tree's prebuilt libraries
   (lib/$MACHTYPE/jkhgap.a, jkweb.a) were months older than the sources, so
   the CGI linked an old botDelay whose behavior did not match botDelay.c.
   Rebuild the libraries after a git pull:
       (cd src/lib && make) ; (cd src/hg/lib && make)


What Layer 3 covers (50 checks)
-------------------------------
Feeds the client one canned middleware response per shape (fixtures, not the
pseudo-random in-browser mock) and asserts what the page shows.

statuses         mapped / unmapped / error cards; mapped-with-no-alignments;
                 missing score+MAPQ shown as a dash with no literal "null";
                 singular vs plural haplotype wording.
haplotypes       representative labelled inline as copyable text and flagged
                 only when it really is a reference; others comma-separated;
                 expander+search appears only for long lists and contains every
                 name; label count; "none reported" when empty.
surjection       ok shows target : position (strand) + CIGAR + scores;
                 position 0 and MAPQ 0 shown as values, not as missing; all
                 five failure states show a human-readable reason, no
                 coordinates and no browser link; a null surjection says "not
                 requested".
browser links    CHM13 -> hs1 and GRCh38 -> hg38 with the 0-based -> 1-based
                 conversion and CIGAR-derived end; no link for sample
                 haplotypes.
mosaic           no bar when num_segments = 1; bar + explanation when > 1; one
                 labelled segment per entry; widths proportional to covered_bp;
                 legend names each representative and haplotype count.
placements       no expander for a single alignment; extra alignments counted
                 under one; primary rendered first even if returned last.
copy/download    surjection copy yields the tab-separated record; haplotype
                 copy yields one name per line; download affordances present;
                 no coordinate copy offered for a failed surjection.
transports       job flow posts cmd=map to our own CGI (never to the
                 middleware), form-encoded, shows a placeholder card and
                 progress, polls with GET + job_id, renders the finished result,
                 clears progress and does not duplicate cards; sync flow
                 renders identically with no polling at all.
partial failure  a mapped, an unmapped and an errored sequence render side by
                 side, and the good one keeps its coordinate.
server errors    an error envelope from the CGI is surfaced with a Retry.

Clipboard assertions work because loadClient.js captures what the client's
hidden-textarea copy would have put on the clipboard (document.copiedText).


Still to come (see the layered plan)
------------------------------------: every response shape and surjection status
         rendered correctly, job vs sync transport, incremental rendering,
         mosaic bar, copy/download text, config-injected-after-script.
Layer 4  Ground-truth round-trips against the live middleware: cut reads from
         known reference coordinates, assert haplotypes, surjected position and
         the browser link land exactly where they should (off-by-one probe).
Layer 5  Negative/security: direct POST bypass, malformed responses, stuck
         jobs, expired job ids, XSS-ish sequence names, auth mismatch.
Layer 6  Non-functional: rate limiting, concurrency/429 behavior, tunnel loss,
         post-deploy smoke test (js/css/trash all 200 on the live vhost),
         cross-browser, accessibility.
